### Page 1 of 6

```text
1
CITY CONTRACT NO.
AGREEMENT
THIS AGREEMENT made and entered into this ______ day of __________________, 2011,
by and between the City of Cheyenne, a municipal corporation of the State of Wyoming (hereinafter
“City” or “Lessor”), and Laramie County School District No. 1, 2800 House Avenue, Cheyenne,
Wyoming, (hereinafter “Lessee”).

NOW, THEREFORE, in consideration of the mutual covenants and conditions contained
herein, it is agreed as follows:
1.
Description of Premises: The City leases to the Lessee the following described  real
property (hereinafter “Premises”).
That portion of the tract of land described in DEED WITHOUT WARRANTY, recorded
in Book 1059, Page 391, located southerly of the south right of way of Cosgriff Court
extended westerly to the easterly right of way of I-25, and northerly of the existing cul-de-
sac at the west end of Talbot Court, but reserving a strip of land, twenty (20) feet in width
along, adjacent and parallel to the easterly right of way of I-25, in Pioneer Park, City of
Cheyenne, Laramie County, Wyoming,  Said parcel containing 1.3 acre more or less.
Said parcel being depicted on Exhibit A attached hereto.
2.
Term: The term of this Agreement shall be for five (5) years beginning on the
date of execution of this lease by City and Lessee.  It is agreed that the City may terminate this
Agreement by providing no less than one (1) year’s written notice to Lessee.
3.
Rent:  The Lessee shall pay as rental for the Premises the sum of Ten Dollars
(10.00) per year, which annual rental shall be paid within thirty (30) days after the execution of
this Agreement, and within thirty (30) days after each anniversary of the execution of this
Agreement.
4.
Permitted Uses: The Premises shall be used by the Lessee for the purposes of
temporary installation, maintenance and use of modular classrooms and related temporary
facilities necessary for customary school services and activities.   The City reserves the right,
upon ten (10) days written notice, to require the Lessee to discontinue any specific use of the
Premises other than purposes stated herein.
5.
Insurance.
a.
Commercial General Liability Insurance.  The Lessee shall provide
coverage against claims for damages for bodily injury, death, and damage to or
destruction of property of others, including loss of use thereof, and including products
```

### Page 2 of 6

```text
2
and completed operations, with minimum limits of One Million Dollars ($1,000,000.00)
per occurrence and Two Million Dollars ($2,000,000.00) aggregate.
b.
The Lessee shall be responsible for securing insurance on  personal
property, owned by the Lessee and others, which will be located in or on the Premises.
c.
The City of Cheyenne shall be named as an additional insured by an
endorsement on the Lessee’s general liability policy for the term of this Agreement.
d.
It is understood and agreed that this policy is primary and not contributory.
 Within thirty (30) days after the execution of this Agreement, the Lessee  shall provide to
the City insurance certificates attesting to the existence of the insurance coverages
required by this Agreement.  All insurance certificates must include a clause stating that
the insurance may not be canceled, amended or allowed to lapse until the expiration of at
least thirty (30) days advance written notice to the City.  The Lessee shall immediately
notify the City of any fact, circumstance, or occurrence that has resulted in or may result
in the cancellation of any insurance coverage required by this Agreement.
e.
The Lessee will report any damage to the property to the City Risk
Manager who will, if necessary, file a claim with the property insurance carrier.  The
Lessee will also advise the City Risk Manager of any liability claim against the Lessee
arising from the use of the Premises.
f.
The Lessee shall pay all federal, state, county and local taxes assessed
against the Premises.
6.
 Governmental Immunity:   The City and Lessee expressly reserves the right to
invoke governmental immunity pursuant to the Wyoming Governmental Claims Act, § 1-39-101,
et seq., with respect to any claims, demands, or causes of action which may be asserted against
the party or parties to this Agreement.
7.
Improvements: The Lessee agrees not to make any improvement, modification or
alteration of the Premises without the express knowledge and written consent of the City of
Cheyenne.  All permanent improvements made to the Premises shall remain with the Premises
and become the property of the City at the expiration of this Agreement.
```

### Page 3 of 6

```text
3
8.
Lessee’s Maintenance Responsibilities:  The Lessee agrees to perform all
reasonable and necessary maintenance of the premises including, but not limited to, compliance
with all provisions of the Cheyenne City Code, state laws, and federal laws which relate to the
use of real property, including protection of the environment.
9.
Liens and Encumbrances: The Lessee agrees not to incur any indebtedness
which will, or may become a lien or encumbrance upon the Premises, nor to allow any mechanic,
builder, materialman, or other claimant to assert any lien against the Premises.  The Lessee
further agrees to discharge any such liens or encumbrances as soon as the same shall have been
asserted against the Premises and shall indemnify and hold the City harmless from the same.
10.
Surrender of Premises at Conclusion of Lease Term: At the conclusion of the
lease period or termination of this Agreement, the Lessee shall return the Premises to the City in
the same condition as received, less reasonable wear and tear.  Unless otherwise directed by the
City, the District shall, upon termination of this Agreement, remove all temporary improvements,
fixtures, equipment, and other personal property placed on the Premises by Lessee.
11.
Assignment: This Agreement may not be assigned without the prior written
consent of the City.
12.
Conformance with Law: The Lessee agrees to comply with all laws in the
performance of this Agreement.
13.
Waiver of Default: No waiver of default by the Lessee of any of the terms,
covenants or conditions hereof  to be performed, kept and observed by the Lessee shall be
construed as, or operate as, a waiver by the City of any subsequent default of any of the terms,
covenants or conditions herein contained to be performed, kept and observed by the Lessee.
14.
Holding Over: The Lessee covenants that at the expiration of the period for
which the Premises are leased to it, or at the earlier termination of this Agreement, it will quit
and surrender the Premises together with fixtures on the property in good state and condition,
reasonable wear and tear excepted.  Should the Lessee hold over the use of or continue to occupy
the Premises after the expiration of the Agreement, such holding over will be as a tenant at
sufferance for which use it shall be liable for any and all damages resulting from such tenancy.
```

### Page 4 of 6

```text
4
15.
Covenant of Quiet Enjoyment: The City covenants for itself, its successors and
assigns that the Lessee, upon payment of the rent and performance of the Lessee’s other
covenants herein, shall and may peaceably and quietly have, hold and enjoy the demised
Premises during the term of this Agreement, provided however, that the City reserves the right to
locate a greenway trail in and along the strip of land, twenty feet (20') feet in width along,
adjacent to and parallel to the easterly right of way of Interstate 25, as set forth in the legal
description above.  In the event the City elects to locate a greenway trail in said strip of land, the
City shall provide ninety (90) days written notice of its intentions to the District.
16.
Notices: Any notices required or given hereunder shall be given by first class
mail, or telegram, addressed to the respective addresses below, or such other address as may be
specified in writing from time to time:
LESSOR
LESSEE
City of Cheyenne
Laramie County School District No. 1.
2101 O’Neil Avenue
2800 House Avenue
Cheyenne, WY 82001
Cheyenne, WY 82001
17.
Eminent Domain: If  the leased property or any part thereof is taken by eminent
domain or sold under the threat of the exercise of said power (all of which are herein called
“condemnation”), this Agreement shall expire on the date when the leased property shall be so
taken, and the rent shall be apportioned as of that date.
18.
Other Agreements.
a.
Declaration of  Governing Law.  This Agreement shall be governed by,
construed and enforced in accordance with the laws of the State of Wyoming.
b.
Parties Have Relationship of Landlord and Tenant- Not Principal-Agent,
Partners or Joint Venturers.  Nothing contained in this Agreement shall be deemed or
construed to create the relationship of principal and agent or of partnership or of a joint
venture or of any association whatsoever between Lessor and Lessee, it being expressly
understood and agreed that neither the computation of rent nor any other provisions
contained in this Agreement nor any act or acts of the parties hereto shall be deemed to
create any relationship between Lessor and Lessee other than relationship of landlord and
tenant.
```

